Baret
[trigger none]
[vignette dungeons/signal_array]

FIXME(mundane): Baret is across from you at the rest circle, holding his teacup with both hands.

FIXME(mundane): You ask him how a Tashkari ends up on a Kesharat crew. He has the answer ready: the pay is steady, the family had a lean year, and a man can take Kesharat coin without taking Kesharat orders. It holds together fine.

FIXME(dread): So you ask how long he has been gone. Since the thaw, he says, one season, this one job. But the nephew he keeps coming back to was born after he left, and the way he describes him the boy is on his feet now with a fistful of words. A child born one season ago is not walking. He cannot have been gone only a season. He says the nephew's name again, pleased, and steps over the arithmetic without seeing it there.

choices:

* Step back to the circle = Let the conversation end
